[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Italian Game"]
[Variation "Rousseau Gambit, 4.Nxe5"]
[ECO "C50"]
[Character "tactical"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "trap,pawn-grab"]
[Refutes "1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 f5 4. Nxe5"]
[Themes "piece-for-pawn,bishop-attacked"]
[Kind "for-us"]

1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 f5 4. Nxe5? { Grabs the pawn, but nothing protects the knight on e5, so Black simply takes it. }
4... Nxe5 { Takes the knight for a pawn, and now the knight attacks the bishop on c4. }
5. Bxg8 ( 5. d4 5... Nxc4 { The pawn attacks the knight, but the knight takes the bishop first, so White has lost two pieces for a pawn. } 6. O-O d5 )
( 5. Bb3 5... fxe4 )
5... Rxg8 { Takes the bishop back: Black has won a knight and a bishop for a knight and a pawn. }
6. d4 6... Ng6 { Steps out of the pawn's way to a safe square and eyes f4 and h4. } 7. O-O 7... fxe4 { Takes the pawn and opens the f-file against the white king. Black is a clear piece up. } *
